      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"glob1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [33, 25, 34]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"glob1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [33, 28, 34]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 3.30 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\n### Step 1: Check Control Conditions\n\n#### Operation 1: `__VERIFIER_assert(glob1 == 0);` at Line 33\n- **Control Condition**: `!(glob1 == 0)`\n  - **Variable Value Tracking**: `glob1` is initialized to `0` at line 17.\n  - **Execution Path Analysis**: In `svp_simple_603_001_main`, `glob1` is checked twice for being `0`. Since `glob1` starts as `0` and there's no modification in `main`, this assertion depends on prior ISR activity.\n\n#### Operation 2: `glob1 = 1;` at Line 25\n- **Control Condition**: `(t == 42)`\n  - **Variable Value Tracking**: `t` is assigned a nondeterministic integer value via `__VERIFIER_nondet_int()` at line 21.\n  - **Execution Path Analysis**: If `t` equals `42`, `glob1` is set to `1`. This condition can be satisfied depending on the value of `t`.\n\n#### Operation 3: `int t = glob1;` at Line 27\n- **Control Condition**: None (direct assignment)\n  - **Variable Value Tracking**: Depends on previous assignments to `glob1`.\n  - **Execution Path Analysis**: Always executed if `isr_1` runs.\n\n#### Operation 4: `glob1 = 0;` at Line 28\n- **Control Condition**: None (direct assignment)\n  - **Variable Value Tracking**: Resets `glob1` to `0`.\n  - **Execution Path Analysis**: Always executed if `isr_1` runs.\n\n#### Operation 5: `__VERIFIER_assert(glob1 == 0);` at Line 34\n- **Control Condition**: `!(glob1 == 0)`\n  - **Variable Value Tracking**: Similar to